nd-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 7pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Total acquisition costs</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="id4f42fc81a614a27b8233f631b1fc49d_D20220101-20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:BusinessCombinationAcquisitionRelatedCosts" scale="3" id="_56d56bc1-1ca2-4a7a-9639-cc8d956a399d">308</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr></table></ix:continuation></div></ix:continuation><div style="text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div id="ibb5d0eb17e77468eb79dc6027d5535b1_154"></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 5 - <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" name="inpx:MergersAcquisitionsAndDispositionsDisclosuresAcquisitionTextBlock" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8xNTQvZnJhZzo1MTAyYzU0Zjk3NzA0NmI0OTM4MDg4NjM2YjY5YTZhNi90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUxMDJjNTRmOTc3MDQ2YjQ5MzgwODg2MzZiNjlhNmE2XzIwMDE_c39fe661-6a92-4618-b3e2-8415de77f795" continuedAt="i659f769396ff4198a865a3d5d241c653" escape="true">Visualix Acquisition</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="i659f769396ff4198a865a3d5d241c653"><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">On April 23, 2021 (the &#8220;Closing Date&#8221;), the Company entered a certain asset purchase agreement by and among the Company, Visualix GmbH i.L. (the &#8220;Visualix&#8221;), Darius Vahdat-Pajouh and Michal Bucko (each, a &#8220;Founder,&#8221; and collectively, the &#8220;Founders&#8221;), and Future Energy Ventures Management GmbH (&#8220;FEVM&#8221;).  </span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Prior to the Closing Date, Visualix owned and operated certain computer vision, robust localization, large-scale navigation, mapping, and 3D reconstruction technologies (collectively, the &#8220;Underlying Technology&#8221;). In accordance with the terms of the asset purchase agreement, the Company purchased from Visualix the entirety of its assets consisting primarily of intellectual property including the underlying technology. Additionally, the Company purchased certain patent applications related to the underlying technology from FEVM.  The Company acquired Visualix to rapidly advance our 3D mapping and to add augmented reality and computer vision capabilities to our product and our product/engineering teams. This innovation is important to our product roadmap and will allow us to stay ahead of the competition.</span></div><div><span><br/></span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In consideration of the transactions (the &#8220;Consideration&#8221;) contemplated by the Asset Purchase Agreement, the Company:</span></div><div style="padding-left:108pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">1.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:10.5pt">remitted a cash payment in the amount of Fifty Thousand Euros (EUR &#8364;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="eur" contextRef="ic703d60b75de43d2a7194c9cf8d01077_D20210423-20210423" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:AssetAcquisitionConsiderationTransferred" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8xNTQvZnJhZzo1MTAyYzU0Zjk3NzA0NmI0OTM4MDg4NjM2YjY5YTZhNi90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUxMDJjNTRmOTc3MDQ2YjQ5MzgwODg2MzZiNjlhNmE2XzEzNDM_abcfa2b7-e466-4b38-ba41-f01945fd8f82">50,000</ix:nonFraction>) to Visualix </span></div><div style="padding-left:108pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">2.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:10.5pt">issued <ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="ic703d60b75de43d2a7194c9cf8d01077_D20210423-20210423" decimals="INF" name="inpx:AssetAcquisitionEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableNumberOfShares" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8xNTQvZnJhZzo1MTAyYzU0Zjk3NzA0NmI0OTM4MDg4NjM2YjY5YTZhNi90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUxMDJjNTRmOTc3MDQ2YjQ5MzgwODg2MzZiNjlhNmE2XzEzNjc_ac3ef34a-f270-41a4-92c4-fada726a6ec6">4,224</ix:nonFraction> shares of Common Stock to Visualix; and</span></div><div style="padding-left:108pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">3.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:10.5pt">issued <ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="ibda55fce561043a2bded0ec3bf47358f_D20210423-20210423" decimals="INF" name="inpx:AssetAcquisitionEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableNumberOfShares" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8xNTQvZnJhZzo1MTAyYzU0Zjk3NzA0NmI0OTM4MDg4NjM2YjY5YTZhNi90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUxMDJjNTRmOTc3MDQ2YjQ5MzgwODg2MzZiNjlhNmE2XzE0MTc_99c890b3-a319-4d8a-8df6-1c5fdc1d9ba6">704</ix:nonFraction> to shares of Common Stock to FEVM.</span></div><div><span><br/></span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">The asset purchase agreement includes customary representations and warranties, as well as certain covenants, including, inter alia, that the Founders are hired as employees of Inpixon GmbH and Visualix and the Founders shall not, for a period of two (<ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ic703d60b75de43d2a7194c9cf8d01077_D20210423-20210423" name="inpx:AssetAcquisitionCovenantsNoncompeteTerm" format="ixt-sec:duryear" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8xNTQvZnJhZzo1MTAyYzU0Zjk3NzA0NmI0OTM4MDg4NjM2YjY5YTZhNi90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUxMDJjNTRmOTc3MDQ2YjQ5MzgwODg2MzZiNjlhNmE2XzE3MDg_ee46ac33-6e27-4cdf-839c-6be52f175fc2">2</ix:nonNumeric>) </span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">years following the Closing Date, directly or indirectly, compete with the Company in the sectors of Mapping and Localization Technology (as defined in the asset purchase agreement).</span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><ix:continuation id="i5f76bd3c80eb47aebed20b7719608ea4" continuedAt="ia08428570142434b94db1aeeaa863d91"><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">The following table represents the purchase price (in thousands). </span></div><div><span><br/></span></div><div><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:79.747%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:18.053%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Cash</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i2784c0225d404ed0a671f18485807608_D20210423-20210423" decimals="-3" name="inpx:PaymentsForAssetAcquisitions" scale="3" id="_f583b792-8f8b-4632-b6c7-055898db3782">61</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"