/span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr style="height:14pt"><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Less discontinued operations</span></td><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">(<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i61490436e74b4c52b7382dbde3133786_I20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLiability" scale="3" id="_a09868e4-7e06-45d7-ba50-c323ba2bc25e">710</ix:nonFraction>)</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Lease liability, continuing operations</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i177baa7b0f6c4396bdd79ceee64278e0_I20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseLiability" scale="3" id="_f8cf6142-b7f8-4709-874f-5a4106f2fa24">545</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr></table></div></ix:nonNumeric><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Operating lease liabilities are based on the net present value of the remaining lease payments over the remaining lease term. In determining the present value of lease payments, the Company used its incremental borrowing rate based on the information available at the date of adoption of Topic 842. As of December&#160;31, 2022, the weighted average remaining lease term is <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ie1b25e2df7ca44beae553be1ddf04901_I20221231" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseWeightedAverageRemainingLeaseTerm1" format="ixt-sec:duryear" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNDcvZnJhZzo0MzVmYzFlNTViMmQ0OGZlOGJlOWNjYmIxM2JkM2QxMy90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjQzNWZjMWU1NWIyZDQ4ZmU4YmU5Y2NiYjEzYmQzZDEzXzI0NDU_567713c4-04db-41c0-9373-746d23b6f239">2.79</ix:nonNumeric> and the weighted average discount rate used to determine the operating lease liabilities was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="ie1b25e2df7ca44beae553be1ddf04901_I20221231" decimals="3" name="us-gaap:OperatingLeaseWeightedAverageDiscountRatePercent" scale="-2" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNDcvZnJhZzo0MzVmYzFlNTViMmQ0OGZlOGJlOWNjYmIxM2JkM2QxMy90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjQzNWZjMWU1NWIyZDQ4ZmU4YmU5Y2NiYjEzYmQzZDEzXzI1NDE_2fd9f216-c524-455c-ba81-60d39b11def7">6.3</ix:nonFraction>%.</span></div></ix:continuation><div id="ibb5d0eb17e77468eb79dc6027d5535b1_250"></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 30 - <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" name="us-gaap:RestructuringAndRelatedActivitiesDisclosureTextBlock" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTAvZnJhZzozYzM2ZDJkM2RkY2U0MzNmOTUxMmJiZjI2NWZhMjkzNS90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjNjMzZkMmQzZGRjZTQzM2Y5NTEyYmJmMjY1ZmEyOTM1Xzk2NQ_274f8db4-f9cb-47ae-9ed8-c28175071934" continuedAt="i093870312b7644468119acf2cef067ab" escape="true">Restructuring Activities</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"><ix:continuation id="i093870312b7644468119acf2cef067ab" continuedAt="ifd0740752bee4804ba907c1f290a9f9c">On September 21, 2022, Inpixon informed its employees that it was taking steps to streamline its operations and conserve cash resources. These steps included layoffs which reduced Inpixon's global employee headcount by approximately <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="i01eb99e0619f4cd9bb2bbe28c3d0dd64_D20220921-20220921" decimals="2" name="us-gaap:RestructuringAndRelatedCostNumberOfPositionsEliminatedPeriodPercent" scale="-2" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTAvZnJhZzozYzM2ZDJkM2RkY2U0MzNmOTUxMmJiZjI2NWZhMjkzNS90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjNjMzZkMmQzZGRjZTQzM2Y5NTEyYmJmMjY1ZmEyOTM1XzI3Mw_b6ad7999-ed27-475c-be86-d41f9faa3200">20</ix:nonFraction>%. The layoffs resulted in one-time expenses of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i0a069bfeb69f47ae90fcc1e6f51a14fe_D20220101-20221231" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:RestructuringCharges" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTAvZnJhZzozYzM2ZDJkM2RkY2U0MzNmOTUxMmJiZjI2NWZhMjkzNS90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjNjMzZkMmQzZGRjZTQzM2Y5NTEyYmJmMjY1ZmEyOTM1XzEwOTk1MTE2Mjg3ODY_59399a09-a5e0-48c5-91e7-ce80c08792f8">0.8</ix:nonFraction> million in the Indoor Intelligence segment which consisted of severance payouts to terminated employees and outplacement service expenses for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022, of which $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i744e251756df4c39925b69a64b87951f_D20220101-20221231" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:RestructuringCharges" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTAvZnJhZzozYzM2ZDJkM2RkY2U0MzNmOTUxMmJiZjI2NWZhMjkzNS90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjNjMzZkMmQzZGRjZTQzM2Y5NTEyYmJmMjY1ZmEyOTM1XzEwOTk1MTE2Mjg4MDQ_e9963609-e7b5-458c-a426-26280a1e8a41">0.7</ix:nonFraction> million pertain to discontinued operations. These expenses were included in the Company's total operating expenses on the </ix:continuation></span></div><div style="height:45pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">F-75</span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:90pt;width:100%"><div><span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">Table of Contents</span></div><div style="margin-top:3pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">INPIXON AND SUBSIDIARIES</span></div><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</span></div><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">FOR THE YEARS ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2022 AND 2021</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 29 - Leases (continued)</span></div></div><ix:continuation id="ifd0740752bee4804ba907c1f290a9f9c"><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Consolidated Statements of Operations with the unpaid restructuring costs included in accrued liabilities in the Consolidated Balance Sheets.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">The Company recorded a Restructuring costs payable for costs incurred related to the restructuring activities noted above for costs incurred but not yet paid as of December&#160;31, 2022.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">  </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfRestructuringReserveByTypeOfCostTextBlock" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTAvZnJhZzozYzM2ZDJkM2RkY2U0MzNmOTUxMmJiZjI2NWZhMjkzNS90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjNjMzZkMmQzZGRjZTQzM2Y5NTEyYmJmMjY1ZmEyOTM1Xzk2Ng_073eb26c-bc18-45c7-87f4-1f1a4530f971" continuedAt="i1eaa6e69b0744ac78f3383665f7b55f1" escape="true">A summary of the activity for the year ended December&#160;31, 2022, is included below (in thousands):</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><ix:continuation id="i1eaa6e69b0744ac78f3383665f7b55f1"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:84.280%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:13.520%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Restructuring costs payable - January 1, 2022</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="ic1bc9cf9dabb422eb1a4bdfce85db9c9_I20211231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:RestructuringReserve" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="3" id="_31c9e03d-e959-4171-872f-658e415654cf">&#8212;</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Restructuring costs incurred</span></td><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:RestructuringCharges" scale="3" id="_0212f45f-0d9f-4152-801c-4ec122752876">845</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Restructuring costs paid</span></td><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">(<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:PaymentsForRestructuring" scale="3" id="_020c3b2e-874e-48ea-a953-c7822c2598fd">793</ix:nonFraction>)</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Restructuring costs payable - December 31, 2022</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="ie1b25e2df7ca44beae553be1ddf04901_I20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:RestructuringReserve" scale="3" id="_a078964f-84ac-4437-b053-9fef7b082cdc">52</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr style="height:15pt"><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Less discontinued operations</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">(<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i61490436e74b4c52b7382dbde3133786_I20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:RestructuringReserve" scale="3" id="_b30180d9-fc3e-48b8-b05a-34910acecb07">52</ix:nonFraction>)</span></td><td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Restructuring costs - continuing operations</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">$</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i177baa7b0f6c4396bdd79ceee64278e0_I20221231" decimals="-3" name="us-gaap:RestructuringReserve" format="ixt:fixed-zero" scale="3" id="_8abcd84c-c631-4662-84fc-edeb596d71c1">&#8212;</ix:nonFraction>&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"></td></tr></table></ix:continuation></div></ix:continuation><div id="ibb5d0eb17e77468eb79dc6027d5535b1_253"></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 31 - <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" name="us-gaap:CommitmentsAndContingenciesDisclosureTextBlock" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTMvZnJhZzozYzhlMDJjZWFkNDg0ZDI4YWM0NWQxNmU1ZjdjYTQ3Ni90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjNjOGUwMmNlYWQ0ODRkMjhhYzQ1ZDE2ZTVmN2NhNDc2XzM0NTE_fdaf1a90-7b98-462c-851d-d2ad1e7e7a3f" continuedAt="i0f8159af33f34c2091c3867dae2bb815" escape="true">Commitments and Contingencies</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="i0f8159af33f34c2091c3867dae2bb815" continuedAt="i62f2b166c180485eb5c73158c6e04e6c"><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Litigation</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Certain conditions may exist as of the date the consolidated financial statements are issued which may result in a loss to the Company, but which will only be resolved when one or more future events occur or fail to occur. The Company assesses such contingent liabilities, and such assessment inherently involves an exercise of judgment. In assessing loss contingencies related to legal proceedings that are pending against the Company, or unasserted claims that may result in such proceedings, the Company evaluates the perceived merits of any legal proceedings or unasserted claims, as well as the perceived merits of the amount of relief sought or expected to be sought therein.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">If the assessment of a contingency indicates that it is probable that a material loss has been incurred and the amount of the liability can be estimated, then the estimated liability would be accrued in the Company&#8217;s consolidated financial statements. If the assessment indicates that a potentially material loss contingency is not probable, but is reasonably possible, or is probable but cannot be estimated, then the nature of the contingent liability and an estimate of the range of possible losses, if determinable and material, would be disclosed.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Loss contingencies considered remote are generally not disclosed, unless they involve guarantees, in which case the guarantees would be disclosed. There can be no assurance that such matters will not materially and adversely affect the Company&#8217;s business, financial position, and results of operations or cash flows. However, the performance of our Company's business, financial position, and results of operations or cash flows may be affected by unfavorable resolution of any particular matter.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Compliance with Nasdaq Continued Listing Requirement</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On October 25, 2021, we received a letter from the Listing Qualifications Staff of The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC (&#8220;Nasdaq&#8221;) indicating that, based upon the closing bid price of our common stock (&#8220;Common Stock&#8221;) for the prior 30 consecutive business days beginning on September 13, 2021, and ending on October 22, 2021, the Company no longer met the requirement to maintain a minimum bid price of $1.00 per share, as set forth in Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2).</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In accordance with Nasdaq Listing Rule 5810(c)(3)(A), we have been provided a period of 180 calendar days, or until April 25, 2022, in which to regain compliance ("Cure Period"). In order to regain compliance with the minimum bid price requirement, the closing bid price of our Common Stock must be at least  $1.00 per share for a minimum of ten consecutive business.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On April 26, 2022, Nasdaq granted us an extension for an additional 180 calendar days beyond the Cure Period, or until October 24, 2022, if we meet the continued listing requirement for market value of publicly held shares and all other initial listing standards for the Nasdaq, with the exception of the bid price requirement, and provide written notice to Nasdaq of our intent to cure the deficiency during this second compliance period, by effecting a reverse stock split, if necessary. </span></div></ix:continuation><div style="height:45pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">F-76</span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:90pt;width:100%"><div><span style="color:#0000ff;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline">Table of Contents</span></div><div style="margin-top:3pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">INPIXON AND SUBSIDIARIES</span></div><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</span></div><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">FOR THE YEARS ENDED DECEMBER 31, 2022 AND 2021</span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"><ix:continuation id="i62f2b166c180485eb5c73158c6e04e6c">We effected a 1-for-75 reverse stock split of our common stock on October 7, 2022, and on November 1, 2022, we were informed by Nasdaq that we have regained compliance with the minimum bid price requirement and that we were back in compliance with the applicable Nasdaq continued listing criteria.</ix:continuation></span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div id="ibb5d0eb17e77468eb79dc6027d5535b1_259"></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Note 32 - <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="ia78dd2c195fb43428268c4e05a3dad19_D20220101-20221231" name="us-gaap:SubsequentEventsTextBlock" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzEzMjQ5_2c501d78-8486-4124-b91b-c2001d1ca51a" continuedAt="i19e45a9dc89b48cba7fc483717016856" escape="true">Subsequent Events</ix:nonNumeric></span></div><ix:continuation id="i19e45a9dc89b48cba7fc483717016856" continuedAt="i894854b0f61f49c7b05e944f4354f357"><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Game Your Game, the Company's subsidiary, entered into a promissory note with an individual whereby it received approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="ic6786c5098514920b66d79e5b9fcb38d_I20230113" decimals="-4" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzE1OQ_06ea9e7d-7320-4a09-9ba8-6943f6008ea8">0.03</ix:nonFraction> million on January 13, 2023 for funding of liabilities and working capital needs. The promissory note has an interest rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="id0e1f099fcae47a6b1c49ca89ebeb98b_I20221231" decimals="2" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzI4MA_23eec268-bf84-4c93-82df-893d9af7c992">8</ix:nonFraction>% and is due on or before June 30, 2023.  </span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">On February 27, 2023, the Company entered into Limited Liability Company Unit Transfer and Joinder Agreements with certain of the Company&#8217;s employees (the &#8220;Transferees&#8221;), pursuant to which (i) the Company transferred all of its Class A Units of CVH (the &#8220;Class A Units&#8221;), an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="i352f93d66f9f41dd81e163375f31db77_D20200101-20201231" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:SaleOfStockNumberOfSharesIssuedInTransaction" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzYxMg_8af2ba9d-1fa2-4900-8e5b-f130389813d1">599,999</ix:nonFraction> Class A Units, to the Transferees as bonus consideration in connection with each Transferee&#8217;s services performed for and on behalf of the Company as an employee, as applicable, which was approved by the board of directors during the quarter ended March 31, 2023 and (ii) each Transferee became a member of CVH and a party to the Amended and Restated Limited Liability Company Agreement of CVH, dated as of September 30, 2020.  </span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">During the quarter ended March 31, 2023, the Company exchanged approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="i9166ae7304e3466994e10221f8fafd7c_D20230101-20230331" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:DebtConversionConvertedInstrumentAmount1" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzExMjA_4bac2a08-3181-418d-8770-f81b085a1202">0.9</ix:nonFraction> million of the outstanding principal and interest under the March 2020 <ix:nonFraction unitRef="number" contextRef="if3a7f33f21444b3cbaa54afc89c12151_I20230331" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzExODY_ab32a849-0c37-4867-a410-10451eca576f">10</ix:nonFraction>% Note Purchase Agreement and Promissory Note for <ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="i299162b29aa643cfb3d363f75657f950_D20230101-20230331" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:DebtConversionConvertedInstrumentSharesIssued1" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzEyMzc_0c5d4e10-e499-488a-8fff-827768df7b2b">611,258</ix:nonFraction> shares of the Company's common stock at prices from $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usdPerShare" contextRef="i54d8902403c94ecdae0eb388dab1fff7_I20230331" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice1" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzEyOTI_0f9d894e-3f43-42e7-8c2c-a0751cdb315f">1.09</ix:nonFraction> to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usdPerShare" contextRef="i288362651bc84f11810360ef387cf0d1_I20230331" decimals="INF" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice1" scale="0" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzEyOTg_3cca639d-a405-4b44-af8b-d4da0d317d7f">1.682</ix:nonFraction> per share, calculated in accordance with Nasdaq's &#8220;minimum price&#8221; as defined by Nasdaq Listing Rule 5635(d).  This note was full satisfied as of January 31, 2023. </span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">During 2023 through the date of this filing, the Company exchanged approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="iad4917587888461a81146242875ac89f_D20230101-20230414" decimals="-5" name="us-gaap:DebtConversionConvertedInstrumentAmount1" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="id3VybDovL2RvY3MudjEvZG9jOmJiNWQwZWIxN2U3NzQ2OGViNzlkYzYwMjdkNTUzNWIxL3NlYzpiYjVkMGViMTdlNzc0NjhlYjc5ZGM2MDI3ZDU1MzViMV8yNTkvZnJhZzo1MGUzZDMxMjJmNmQ0NjQxOWUxY2RiODk4YjI0YWIwMC90ZXh0cmVnaW9uOjUwZTNkMzEyMmY2ZDQ2NDE5ZTFjZGI4OThiMjRhYjAwXzE1NDY_51589087-25f5-4de1-91c8-fce540ccecbe">1.1</ix:nonFraction> million of the outstanding principal and interest under the July 2022 Note Purchase Agreement and Promissory Note for <ix:nonFraction unitRef="shares" contextRef="if8655497e4d4420fadf82b